# A click with nothing asking to hear about it, which is a click the terminal
# keeps: at a shell prompt the mouse is nobody else's business.
mouse press left 3 1
mouse release left 3 1
# The sequence that asks, and a click right behind it. That click is already
# read by the new rule, which is the whole of why the branch is decided beside
# the terminal rather than above it — a mode carried out to the app would
# still be saying "off" here. SGR format, because X10 cannot say which button
# was let go of.
out "\x1b[?1000h\x1b[?1006h"
mouse press left 3 1
mouse release left 3 1
# What was held goes into the button code, so a modifier is not lost on the
# way down.
mouse press right 0 0 ctrl
mouse release right 0 0 ctrl
# Normal tracking reports no motion at all, whatever is held.
mouse motion left 5 1
# Button-event tracking does. The second motion over the cell the first one
# already reported says nothing: a trackpad drags in pixels and a terminal is
# told in cells, so the encoder holds the last one.
out "\x1b[?1002h"
mouse motion left 5 1
mouse motion left 6 1
mouse motion left 6 1
